{#- THE ACTIVATION MATRIX, v1 — Portuguese sibling of /members/activacion/.
    Same 8 routines, same library structure; only the copy changes.

    Original note follows.

    THE ACTIVATION MATRIX, v1 — replaces the two fixed activation tools that
    lived at this URL and at /members/activacion-ciclismo/ (both retired
    Aug 13, 2026 on Iván's call). Home doc: `activation-matrix.md`.

    Three questions → one of 8 routines (sport × moment × equipment). The
    tightness axis is v2 and deliberately absent; see the home doc.

    Structure: one exercise LIBRARY, and 8 routines that are just lists of ids.
    That is the whole point of the design — 8 lists and a lookup, never 8
    hand-written routines, because the 12 exercises they share must not drift
    into 12 slightly different cues.

    The engine (activation-tool.js) is unchanged. It boots off
    window.ACTIVATION_DATA, so this page builds that object after the athlete
    answers and only then injects the engine script — which is why the partial
    is included with `matrixMode`.

    *** v1.1, Sept 3, 2026 — SWIMMING added as a third sport, mirroring the
    Spanish page. 14 routines, not 12: swimming has three equipment options
    where run and bike have two, so the grid is 4 + 4 + 6. Home doc:
    `activation-matrix.md` §v1.1, which owns the reasoning for all of it.

    Two structural changes came with it:
      1. The equipment question is SPORT-AWARE — a mini-band is the right
         question for run and bike and the wrong object for swimming. EQUIP
         holds the options per sport; switching sport also RESETS the answer,
         because swim|..|stick exists and run|..|stick does not.
      2. Phase names live in each routine, not in build(). Run and bike go
         floor → knees → standing; swimming warms up standing, drops to the
         floor, and finishes standing on the stroke.

    *** CLINICAL: stick DISLOCATES are deliberately not here. The source doc
    called them indispensable for opening the anterior capsule; competitive
    swimmers are typically lax there, not stiff, and short of internal rotation
    — which is what the swimmer's-shoulder tool is built around. What ships
    instead is a capped pass-through that stops at the first compensation. Do
    not restore dislocates. ***

    *** GUARDRAIL: methodology.md says Iván does not teach swimming. The catch
    simulation primes the feel of pressure; it must never become stroke
    instruction. ***

    *** EVERY NOTE ABOUT THIS PAGE BELONGS IN THIS BLOCK. Almost the entire
    page is inside a raw block, and Nunjucks comments are NOT comments in
    there — they are literal text and they render to the reader. Two did
    exactly that on the Spanish page on Sept 3, 2026. `automation/build-sanity.js`
    now asserts no template delimiters survive into any built HTML. -#}
